  "text": "Board of Elections \u2013 Jones County, North Carolina | Official Website\nSkip to content\nMenu\nAbout\nAbout Jones County\nQuality of Life\nJones County History\nEvents\nNews\nGovernment\nBoard of Commissioners\nCommissioner Agendas and Minutes\nCounty Manager\u2019s Office\nOrdinances\nBudgets, Audits and Financial Information\nBids and RFPS\nGoverning Boards\nCounty Holidays\nCommunity Closet\nNewsletter\nUrgent Repair Program\nDepartments\nA-L\nAdministration\nBoard of Elections\nVoter Registration\nElections Schedule\nJones County Voting Precincts and Locations\nAbsentee Voting\nElection Results\nCounty Commissioner District FAQs\nCandidates\nFee Schedule\nFrequently Asked Questions\nCivic Center\nCivic Center FAQ\nCooperative Extension\nEconomic Development\nCommittee of 100\nCounty Resources\nJones County Industrial Park\nMaysville Development Corporation Industrial Park\nJones County Directory of Local Businesses\nEmergency Services\nEmergency Medical Services\nFire Marshal Services\nEmergency Management\nFinance\nHealth Department\nAdvisory Committee on Health\nClinical Services\nWomen, Infants & Children Program\nHealth Education\nSchool Nurse Program\nPublic Health Preparedness\nEnvironmental Health\nRecovery and Re-Entry Support\nContacts\nHuman Resources\nCareers\nInspections\nM-Z\nRecreation\nRegister of Deeds\nFrequently Asked Questions\nFee Schedule\nUniform Commercial Code Information\nFiling an Assumed Business Name\nNotary Information\nSenior Services\nSheriff\u2019s Office\nConcealed Weapon Permits\nJones County Detention Center\nSex Offenders\nFingerprints\nDNA Samples\nSocial Services\nSoil & Water Conservation\nSolid Waste\nTax Department\nAddressing\nReal Property\nIndividual and Business Personal Property\nRegistered Motor Vehicles\nVehicle Registration Gap Billing\nProperty Tax Relief\nFrequently Asked Questions\nPresent-Use Value Program\nVeteran\u2019s Services\nWater\nNews\nFind\nCivic Center\nContact Information\nEducation Links\nEvents\nGIS Mapping\nJob Openings\nBids and RFPS\nLatest News\nOnline Tax Payments\nOnline Water Payments\nTowns\nMaysville\nPollocksville\nTrenton\nQuick Links:\nCareers\nEvents\nCommissioners\nAgendas & Minutes\nContact\nFacebook\nOpen Search Window\nHome\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\nClick here to view 2026 candidates lists.\nQUICK LINKS:\nBoard of Elections Home\n|\n2026 Election Information\n|\nAbsentee Voting\n|\nCandidates\n|\nCounty Commissioner District FAQs\n|\nEarly Voting & Same Day Registration\n|\nElection Results\n|\nElection Schedule\n|\nFee Schedule\n|\nFrequently Asked Questions\n|\nPrecinct Officials\n|\nVoter Fraud\n|\nVoter ID Information\n|\nVoter Registration\n|\nVoting Locations\n|\nVoting Systems\nNCSBE Registration Repair Project: Click here to find out more about the North Carolina effort to obtain missing indentification information and fix deficient voter registrations.\nAbout Us\nThe Jones County Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all federal, state and local elections held within Jones County and maintaining registered voter information.\nThe Jones County Elections Department operates under the guidance of the five-member Jones County Board of Elections. The board is composed of two Democrats, two Republicans, and a Chair appointed by the Governor. Board members are nominated by local political parties and appointed by the State Board of Elections for a two-year term. While elections personnel are county employees, the Elections Director is appointed by the State Board of Elections based on the recommendation of the Jones County Board of Elections.\nThe Board of Elections is committed to ensuring that the electoral process is conducted fairly and honestly and that all election laws, campaign finance laws, rules and regulations are equally applied.\nServices Include:\nMaintain voter registration records for the county and three municipalities\nReceive candidate filing for General Assembly and local candidates\nReceive, audit, and maintain campaign finance reports for local candidates/committees\nProvide for remote absentee voting\nRecruit, appoint, and train all election day officials\nEstablish all election precincts and provide election day voting\nReport election day results to public and authorities\nEvaluate and improve election services\nProvide election reports and statistical information\nContract for and maintain polling places\nMaintain and store all voting equipment\nInvestigate all any voting irregularities\nOther Community Services Include:\nProvide voter and precinct information to the public\nProvide registration materials and advice for community registration drives\nVisit community groups for voter/election education\n2025-2027\nBoard Members\nThe County Board of Elections operates under a five-member board that is appointed every two years. The board is two Democrats, two Republicans, and a Chair that is appointed by the State Auditor, effective December 11, 2024 (\nSession Law 2024-57\n).\nRobert E. Jolly, Chairman (R)\nNellie F, Brown, Secretary (D)\nKristin B. Betzel (R)\nClifton D. Gray (R)\nZack A. Koonce, III (D)\nBoard Meetings\nRegular monthly meetings are held the first Tuesday of each month at 1 p.m. in the Board of Elections Office located at 367 NC Hwy 58 South, Unit B, Trenton, NC 28585.\n2026 Board Meeting Schedule\nLogic & Accuracy Testing: September 22, 2026, 10 a.m.\nNext Meeting (Absentee): September 29, 2026, 1 p.m.\nMeeting Agendas\n2025-2027 Chief Judges and Judges\nList of Chief Judges and Judges\nAdditional Resources\nJones County Elected Officials\nVR Statistics by Precinct\nNCSBE Voter Registration Statistics Tool\n2026 General Election UOCAVA Notice\nJones County\nBoard of Elections\n367 Hwy 58 S, Unit B\nTrenton, NC 28585\nPhone: 252-448-3921\nFax: 252-448-1040\nFollow us on Facebook\nDirector:\nSheila Garner\nHours of Operation\nMonday-Thursday\n8am-5pm\nFridays\n8am-Noon\nJones County Government\n110 S Market Street\nTrenton, NC 28585\nPhone: 252-448-7571\nMonday \u2013 Thursday, 8:00am\u20135:00pm\nFriday, 8:00am-12:00pm\nSearch for:\nSearch\nLiving Here\nNews\nEvents\nAbout Jones County\nOur History\nGovernment\nCommissioners\nAgendas & Minutes\nCounty Departments\nManager\u2019s Office\nCounty Boards\nQuick Links\nJob Openings\nGIS Mapping\nTax Payments\nWater Payments\nCivic Center\nFacebook\nOpen Search Window\nSmall Living. Big Opportunity.\nPrivacy Policy\nSitemap\nNon-Discrimination Statement\nContact\n\u00a9 2026 Jones County, North Carolina | Official Website \u2022 All Rights Reserved. Website by\nEdge360 Creative\n.\nSearch for:\nSearch\nClose Search Window\n\u2191",
